   "feed_anfang": "Your Azure OpenAI and Copilot Studio bills keep climbing even when usage looks flat. This episode is for architects, platform teams and FinOps leads running AI agents in the Microsoft cloud, and it shows how to find the context, reasoning and autonomous taxes and remove them with caching, compression, routing and governance.<br /><br /><b>In this episode</b><br /><ul><li>00:00 – Three hidden taxes and the four billing layers</li><li>03:15 – The context tax and the reasoning tax</li><li>09:03 – The autonomous tax and the November 2026 credit cliff</li><li>11:40 – Auditing spend: Cost Management, consumption estimator and token flow maps</li><li>21:10 – Four levers: semantic caching, LLMLingua compression, model routing, PTU vs PAYG</li><li>36:57 – Guardrails, the 90-day roadmap and the governance model</li><li>61:48 – Case study: rebuilding the Contoso support agent</li><li>71:00 – Advanced scenarios, emergency brakes and the weekly checklist</li></ul><br /><b>Key takeaways</b><br /><ul><li>Most AI agent cost comes from architecture, not model pricing: bloated retrieval context, sending every request to the flagship model, and autonomous agents consuming <a href=\"https://www.m365.fm/entity/copilot-credits/?utm_source=podcast&utm_medium=shownotes&utm_campaign=how-to-architect-low-cost-ai-agents-in-the-microsoft-cloud\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Copilot credits</a> unchecked.</li><li>Four levers compound when applied together: semantic caching in Azure API Managem",
